==Enemy==
Othom has more damage and health than both [[Mooth]] and [[Maawth]], with an [[Omni Strike]] that hits cats up to 440 range away from him, outranging the majority of non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] units.

As with most Relic enemies, Othom also has a 100% chance to [[Curse|curse]], but its meager 2-second duration means it isn't too much of an issue, except in [[Rutsborg Vortex]], where Othom debuts and is supported by [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], as the curse cripples your [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cats]] for the pushers to advance. He is also very tanky, especially for a backliner, with 800,000 HP and only one knockback.

At higher strength magnifications, Othom can have up to around 1.6 million HP, 24,000 damage and 8k DPS. His HP buff is actually quite negligible since he still only has one knockback and can't reposition, but his attack becomes strong enough to kill a maxed [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] in two hits instead of three, along with many more interaction changes, which require higher level units to counter properly.

==Strategy==
Thanks to his [[Omni Strike]], most cheap attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] become obsolete, so use cats that can outrange him such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] and/or [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], as they can hit Othom from a safe distance. You could also use [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], but only if they outrange Othom or if they can exploit their Long Distance without him hitting them, with [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] being the prime example on higher difficulties. Certain long-ranged [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] like [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Catman]] (who also does massive damage to Relics) or [[Kintaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Kinrangers GigaForce]], should you be lucky enough to have them, will also be helpful. Since he only has one knockback, the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] can aid in keeping him at bay. Talented [[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Uesugi Kenshin]] can work as well, but her knockback may do more harm than help in some situations, as it lets Othom reposition. However, she does pretty well regardless.

When there's an opening to attack Othom, a [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is an unusual but usable counter that exploits Othom's Floating trait. Because of Othom's relatively low damage and curse uptime, Fishman Cat's foreswing will usually finish right as the Curse effect wears off and allowing the Massive Damage trait to take effect. Conversely, this will not work if Fishman Cat's Move Speed Up [[Talents|Talent]] has been unlocked, as Fishman will then hit Othom while still being Cursed unless something else preemptively Curses Othom. [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] is another rusher whose massive damage to Relics can serve well to cripple Othom, and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]'s Curse Immunity Talent can also help it keep him at bay with weaken.

